# =====================================================
# IMPORTANT CONCEPTS
# =====================================================

# 1. SPACE COMPLEXITY
"""
Time Complexity  = How execution time grows with input
Space Complexity = How memory usage grows with input

Example: Creating new array of size n → O(n) space
Example: Using single variable → O(1) space
"""

# 2. BEST/AVERAGE/WORST CASE
"""
- Best Case (Ω): Minimum time needed
  Example: First element found → Ω(1)
  
- Average Case (Θ): Expected time  
  Example: Middle element found → Θ(n/2) → Θ(n)
  
- Worst Case (O): Maximum time needed
  Example: Last element found → O(n)
"""

# 3. DROP CONSTANTS & NON-DOMINANT TERMS
"""
RULE 1 - Drop Constants:
O(2n) → O(n)
O(100) → O(1)
O(5n²) → O(n²)

RULE 2 - Keep Highest Order:
O(n² + n) → O(n²)
O(n³ + n²) → O(n³)
O(5n³ + 10n² + 100n) → O(n³)
"""

# 4. RECURSION COMPLEXITY
def factorial(n):
    if n <= 1: 
        return 1
    return n * factorial(n-1)  
    # Time: O(n) - makes n recursive calls
    # Space: O(n) - call stack stores n frames

